feedback.suggestion:
Replace execAsync with process.execFile() to avoid shell interpretation. Example:

await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
  const child = execFile('redis-cli', [
    '-h', redisHost,
    '-p', redisPort,
    ...(redisPassword ? ['-a', redisPassword] : []),
    'lpush',
    `cfn-completion:${taskId}`,
    agentMetadata
  ], (error) => {
    if (error) reject(error);
    else resolve(undefined);
  });
});

Add explicit Redis connectivity check before attempting coordination:

const checkRedis = async () => {
  try {
    await execAsync(`redis-cli -h "${redisHost}" -p "${redisPort}" ${authFlag} PING`);
  } catch (error) {
    throw new Error(`Redis connectivity check failed at ${redisHost}:${redisPort} - ensure Redis is running`);
  }
};

